      "content": "yeah valgrind is a bit heavy for this specific hardware setup since it's an ARM-based microcontroller with limited resources. i'm mostly limited to using static analysis or maybe some custom instrumentation in the heap allocator. the thing is, the leak is so gradual and intermittent that it's almost impossible to pinpoint. it feels like every time i fix one thing, another small piece of memory just disappears. any ideas for a more lightweight way to catch these tiny, hidden leaks?",
